{"title":"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Ptolemy&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Ptolemy's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Coordinate_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Coordinate Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Trig_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Trig Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Rectangular_Construction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Rectangular Construction)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">Square</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">points</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are exterior to the square such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76da12e48800da8c07b5ee4bb4cf8e4233af20a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=DF=5$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19deffd3bef40f52facec45a3e82c807a1fe91d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=CF=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0045947c9898a2f8b1def2e032e79bbc85185305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF^{2}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/cafdb94a2b1b9ade43e0c5225cb0329c449cd7b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(0.2 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, F;  A = (0,13); B = (13,13); C = (13,0); D = (0,0); E = A + (12*12/13,5*12/13); F = D + (5*5/13,-5*12/13);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--E--B); draw(C--F--D);  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(0)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(0)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, N); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S);[/asy]\" width=\"175\" height=\"255\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb5aad8985139387c524a789ebfc9881a16fe3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FCD = \\alpha$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7d741bdd83541fd43f70743b25a563e5255ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FB = \\sqrt{12^2 + 13^2 + 2\\cdot12\\cdot13\\sin(\\alpha)} = \\sqrt{433}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"356\" height=\"32\" />. By the diagonal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2564f730e0220dbe7c4de64990613b32ec4bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB = 13\\sqrt{2}, DB^2 = 338$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><b>The sum of the squares of the sides of a parallelogram is the sum of the squares of the diagonals.</b>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff9c1e6d8c42d54ddd5fd5c2bb27a7e88c2b201.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EF^2 = 2\\cdot(5^2 + 433) - 338 = 578.\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4552f6683b9d84eb10ebea00e5a8f9d3c69186b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}, \\overline{DF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca0738020ed7778340f9f10decfd1af9b26e9338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}, \\overline{CF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" /> to their points of intersection. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca3030752ba9dd8871ea7764b5aa4bd2c180c6f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE \\cong \\triangle CDF$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" /> and are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangles</a>, we can come to the conclusion that the two new triangles are also congruent to these two (use <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Congruent_(geometry)#ASA_Congruence\">ASA</a>, as we know all the sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the angles are mostly complementary). Thus, we create a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caff379825b8ed5e366c1e8cdb8bda7eaece1c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 12 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd75b0b5f2740c3766ea40dc5063e2381c70c247.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(0.25 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H;  A = (0,13); B = (13,13); C = (13,0); D = (0,0); E = A + (12*12/13,5*12/13); F = D + (5*5/13,-5*12/13); G = rotate(90,(A + C)/2)*(E); H = rotate(90,(A + C)/2)*(F);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(E--G--F--H--cycle);  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(0)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, N); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, W); dot(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, dir(0));[/asy]\" width=\"315\" height=\"308\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0f6a692f19a65fe60fe5745826792f3fd1d57e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is the diagonal of the square, with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e385e910e2af35491c696c426c1c1a1223df71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />; the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c975b5b1bae67ab12e37a55f047fcb24c0b355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF^2 = (17\\sqrt{2})^2 = 578$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A slightly more analytic/brute-force approach:\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AIME_II_prob10_bruteforce.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/59/AIME_II_prob10_bruteforce.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"398\" height=\"506\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Drop perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, respectively; construct right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f177f5d2a2060c3367173b3e2d5c5fdd1abf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EKF$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> with right angle at K and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a948b820901bac187aaf18089af396be84fbf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EK || BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e74fabd72a3055573cdae880ca96865e528909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2[CDF]=DF*CF=CD*JF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/36323b14a16da1463993f476e130b8170a112388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JF=5\\times12/13 = \\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c12e140c1c1460c8e7b87758b0a85d445250e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI=\\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/9102c900030e8dc1488dc30268a22e0c830390f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DJF \\sim \\triangle DFC$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b4cc2313ba4f309bd4b5f750f5817fd0e67f046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DJ=\\frac{5JF}{12}=\\frac{25}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/3/7a36fd29ad73d25987c4a164c6294b19c7ccdec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FK=DC-(DJ+IB)=DC-2DJ=13-\\frac{50}{13}=\\frac{119}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"448\" height=\"38\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88c21291c0049822528e9d30c289736c8ca27318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EK=BC+(JF+IE)=BC+2JF=13+\\frac{120}{13}=\\frac{289}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"453\" height=\"38\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f031ed561a8e3806c761ef2cc4796f46f84baad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{289}{13}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{119}{13} \\right)^2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{(17^2)(17^2+7^2)}}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"385\" height=\"53\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/8076439ce284384077042610e5673cd931c12190.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{17\\sqrt{338}}{13}=\\frac{17(13\\sqrt{2})}{13}=17\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"254\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e93753c8bbac469586a18d9949332953443322d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF^2=(17\\sqrt{2})^2=578$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Based on the symmetry, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> across the center of the square, which we will denote as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27eb4aaf9094e908fde4035bd17ecdaaf591516b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f76e209ba6efb92105415d4f3c62ef804a52519d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> are right, we can conclude that figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c44f49e06dd3891792587f13b7a7798a990cf51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOBE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral. Pythagorean Theorem yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/4915676addc2fbe47deacf3df20c8c77309896f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO=AO=\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"41\" />. Now, using Ptolemy's Theorem, we get that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e962e0eeff8a5fef1870bbcb7f25086aa4a29a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AO\\cdot BE + BO\\cdot AE = AB\\cdot AO\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b2805d4fbc5781ad5b37f1723b0cb6e78fedfd1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 5+\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 12 = 13\\cdot OE\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/73339f8739e27ff47b1aed00b7fcc698e134a4ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OE=\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />\nNow, since we stated in the first step that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a339dc21c03223ff913127611d8c832eac8e7053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=2EO=17\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />. This gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b377e814449cfd4f60117f7d0d3403b8f1c68b8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EF^2=(17\\sqrt{2})^2=578\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" /> AWD with this bash solution\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Ptolemy.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Ptolemy's_Theorem)\">Solution 5 (Ptolemy's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Drawing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, it clearly passes through the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Letting this point be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/49764141605f6f669bfc750b4f3e998d21449a2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEBP$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d27a1a3030826dbcdb54fb68101dc44540cf266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFDP$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> are congruent cyclic quadrilaterals, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1c41d137808b8544b04437663ef833fdb531bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=BP=CP=DP=\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"243\" height=\"42\" /> Now, from Ptolemy's, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef0dd29353fad30745ced4b27028455b64f9818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\cdot EP=\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{2}}(12+5)\\implies EP=\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"327\" height=\"48\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d0ffcc2071235d6054a5d0b8907d22dc75d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=EP+FP=2\\cdot EP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"14\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d63b37a1d1fe6dadd19eb8cd95468d3ba9ddb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(17\\sqrt{2})^2=\\boxed{578}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Coordinate_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Coordinate_Bash)\">Solution 6 (Coordinate Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Coordinate Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Place the vertices of the square as follows:\n\\begin{align}\nD &amp;= (0,\\;0),\\\\\nC &amp;= (13,\\;0),\\\\\nA &amp;= (0,\\;13),\\\\\nB &amp;= (13,\\;13).\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>Compute the coordinates of points E and F using the distance formula.\nPlace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>\\begin{aligned}\nx^2+(y-13)^2 = 144,\\\\\n(x-13)^2+(y-13)^2 = 25\n\\end{aligned}\n</p><p>\\begin{aligned}\na^2+b^2=25,\\\\\n(a-13)^2+b^2=144.\n\\end{aligned}\n</p><p>Solving and taking appropriate solutions to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a024fa97ff46aa5c6831c57ce4d5a28466527da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (144/13,229/13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />, and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2526cb99aff34bf81a47b8cc2ab47c19b5bbfa87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F = (25/13, -60/13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Computing distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e385e910e2af35491c696c426c1c1a1223df71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6e8a779ccc83a53379cc02f9ba0348b81d766d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EF^2 = 578\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Trig_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Trig_Bash)\">Solution 7 (Trig Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Trig Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We first see that the whole figure is symmetrical and reflections across the center that we will denote as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> bring each half of the figure to the other half. Thus we consider a single part of the figure, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d09bb7adcc1ff2fd29436e73d279777c8aa3d5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EO.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>First note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e27362bac28d080cc09cc66ac244971e4500dec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAO = 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae54b43c219341de4a6e5919922cf55371e6ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a304821acbd12497d35ebdd7633565367df14c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAB = \\arccos{\\left(\\frac{12}{13}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606ab580ac6d81e27b98c120d168009127cf58f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{5}{13}\\right)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" /> Finally, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a0cddcd862a52a8e6173ea36770e0d5e510997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO =\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"43\" /> Now we apply laws of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0920da223b05402ae7c60a3981d417a372b68108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup AEO.$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/7263223b37ea661f0c4283486aec6a7621adb314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EO^2 = 12^2 + (\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2})^2 - 2 \\cdot 12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\cdot \\cos{\\angle EAO}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"426\" height=\"53\" /> We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31cd2a060eccbca6ea3de321477004df42ef289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAO = 45^{\\circ} + \\arccos{\\left(\\frac{12}{13}\\right)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"231\" height=\"43\" /> Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bd1242b7362fa2a71468c8c87648bb4ea8df1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\angle EAO} = \\cos\\left(45^{\\circ} + \\arccos{\\left(\\frac{12}{13}\\right)}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"305\" height=\"43\" /> which applying the cosine sum identity yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d97b16ed1412e65be6d2397e2f2d083c1da8c0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{45^{\\circ}}\\cos{\\arccos\\frac{12}{13}} - \\sin{45^{\\circ}}\\sin\\arcsin{\\frac{5}{12}} =\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{26} -\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{26} =\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{26}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"526\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>Note that we are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c3be6a81536f56bdace99bbd45edc2e34e1ac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4EO^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> so we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a9ea2b9ebcf6fe37729ebdddf76c9f252c6eee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EO^2 = 12^2 + \\left(\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2 - 2 \\cdot 12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\cdot \\cos{\\angle EAO}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"435\" height=\"56\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> obtaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0840d568e5bc39d45792312c0645b0dd21a526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4EO^2 = 576 + 338 - 8 \\cdot\\left(\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\cdot 12 \\cdot\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{26} = 576 + 338 - 4  \\cdot 12 \\cdot  7 = \\boxed{578}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"599\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Rectangular_Construction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Rectangular_Construction)\">Solution 8 (Rectangular Construction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Rectangular Construction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007aimeiiq3s8.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b8/2007aimeiiq3s8.png/350px-2007aimeiiq3s8.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"533\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/b8/2007aimeiiq3s8.png 1.5x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Construct a rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> as shown above starting with the top left vertex, moving clockwise about the blue box. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/94424b9ee66f541a9a0055df18bbcae8ce691e1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB&#39; = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c339e0aaa9fe13c81316db2dff52a5c80f213cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;B = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba80718299b521451878b6d8d86550aa4c9b7d06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA&#39; = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />. Through <b>CPCTC</b> it follows that most other side lengths due to congruence are equal to one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Three equations arise, particularly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee9210dd6f444db6a5e78d3e26bef88d86f91a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 13, a^2 + c^2 = 25, b^2 + c^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"301\" height=\"20\" />, which we can easily solve to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5ac1bfae5cf27539d31df09e2d5bdb708ed0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{25}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44491ca497eb87d7de3403787792349fca22a8a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{144}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850464da124fa8623ba2013f6ea1efdbf364726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> (negate negative solution). Drop the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1eb0abeec6f6ca0a4a6cbd2891e2e421d3c3202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/63879477e71d3e4ed6fa6716a2a655843e4fb032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FGE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is right with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da037a030677a701754d0307556c25015f432004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a=\\frac{144-25}{13}=\\frac{119}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d66a36d38d230ea28d72772ce9b336dbe3654e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13+2c=\\frac{289}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />, so solving via substitution and Pythagorean yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/0359783afc727d66c55339193e5f5fc379d6cf67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = \\frac{\\sqrt{97682}}{13} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{578}}{13} = \\sqrt{578}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"275\" height=\"43\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b69b84372dad5de07353d9750e8007d83532e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF^2 = \\boxed{578}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II\" title=\"2007 AIME II\">2007 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2007\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"200